= Solution
{parent=1f}

The Leibniz definition is
$$\det A=\sum_{\pi\in S_n}\operatorname{sgn}(\pi)\prod_{i=1}^nA_{i,\pi(i)}.$$
The adjugate is the transpose of the cofactor <matrix>. Cofactor expansion gives
$$A\operatorname{adj}(A)=\operatorname{adj}(A)A=(\det A)I.$$
For the displayed tridiagonal <matrix>, expansion along the last row gives $D_n=2D_{n-1}-D_{n-2}$, with $D_1=2,D_2=3$. Induction yields
$$\det A_n=D_n=n+1.$$

