$$f(z)-f(w)=f'(z_0)(z-w)+\int_w^z(f'(\zeta)-f'(z_0))\,d\zeta.$$
The second term has <modulus> strictly below $|f'(z_0)||z-w|$, so the sum cannot vanish. Thus $f$ is one-to-one.

